{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftExplain"}],"role":"collectionGroup","title":"SHAP & LIME Model Interpretability","roleHeading":"API Collection"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Explain machine learning model predictions with game-theoretic Shapley value attributions (TreeSHAP, KernelSHAP) and local linear surrogates (LIME)."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/ModelInterpretability"],"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/ShapleyAttributions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Black-box machine learning models—such as deep neural networks, random forests, and gradient boosting trees—produce accurate predictions but obscure the individual feature contributions that drove a particular decision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftExplain"},{"text":" provides mathematically grounded, axiomatic interpretability algorithms:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": Fast, exact polynomial-time Shapley attributions for tree-based models ("},{"code":"DecisionTreeClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"RandomForestClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"RandomForestRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") adhering to the four Shapley efficiency and consistency axioms."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","isActive":true}]},{"type":"text","text":": Model-agnostic explainer solving constrained weighted linear regression against an empirical background dataset for any arbitrary asynchronous prediction function."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations fitting ridge linear surrogate models around perturbed neighborhoods.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"code":["graph TD","    Model[Trained Model \/ Ensemble] --> ModelType{Model Architecture}","    ModelType -->|Tree Ensemble \/ Forest| Tree[TreeSHAP: Exact Lundberg Algorithm]","    ModelType -->|Arbitrary Black-Box \/ Pipeline| Kernel[KernelSHAP: Empirical Regression]","    ModelType -->|Local Linear Surrogate| LIME[LIMEExplainer: Perturbation Neighborhood]","    Tree --> Attributions[Exact Shapley Values: sum phi_i = f(x) - E(f)]","    Kernel --> Attributions","    LIME --> SurrogateWeights[Local Coefficients + R^2 Goodness of Fit]","    Attributions --> FeatureRanking[Feature Importance Ranking & Waterfall Breakdown]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"mermaid"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"1-Exact-TreeSHAP-for-Tree-Ensembles","text":"1. Exact TreeSHAP for Tree Ensembles","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"TreeSHAP (Lundberg et al., 2018; Nature Machine Intelligence) optimizes exponential subset evaluation into polynomial time $O(T L D^2)$ by recursively tracking conditional expectations along decision tree splitting paths."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftML","import SwiftExplain","","\/\/ 1. Train a Random Forest model on feature data","let rf = RandomForestClassifier(nEstimators: 50, maxDepth: 6)","try await rf.fit(features: X_train, targets: y_train)","","\/\/ 2. Initialize TreeSHAP explainer","let treeShap = TreeSHAP()","","\/\/ 3. Compute exact Shapley attributions for an individual observation","let testInstance = X_test[0]","let shapValues = await treeShap.explain(randomForest: rf, instance: testInstance)","","\/\/ 4. Rank features by absolute impact on the decision","let featureNames = [\"Income\", \"DebtToIncome\", \"CreditScore\", \"EmploymentYears\", \"LoanAmount\"]","let ranked = zip(featureNames, shapValues).sorted { abs($0.1) > abs($1.1) }","","print(\"Feature attributions for instance:\")","for (name, phi) in ranked {","    let direction = phi >= 0 ? \"+\" : \"-\"","    print(\"  • \\(name): \\(direction)\\(String(format: \"%.4f\", abs(phi)))\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Concurrent-Batch-Explanations","text":"Concurrent Batch Explanations","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For dataset-wide interpretability or global summary plots, compute attributions concurrently across Apple Silicon CPU cores:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let flatTrees = await rf.flatTrees","let batchAttributions = await treeShap.explainBatch(","    trees: flatTrees,","    instances: X_test,","    numFeatures: featureNames.count",")","print(\"Computed SHAP matrix for \\(batchAttributions.count) instances.\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"2-Model-Agnostic-Explanations-with-KernelSHAP","text":"2. Model-Agnostic Explanations with `KernelSHAP`","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When interpreting models without tree structures—such as support vector machines, neural decoders, or multi-stage pipelines—","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP"},{"text":" estimates Shapley values through weighted linear regression over coalition permutations:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftExplain","","\/\/ 1. Initialize KernelSHAP explainer actor","let kernelShap = KernelSHAP()","","\/\/ 2. Compute Shapley attributions using background baseline dataset","let attributions = await kernelShap.explain(","    model: { features in","        \/\/ Any asynchronous prediction function mapping [Double] -> Double","        return await myNeuralNetwork.predict(features)","    },","    instance: testInstance,","    background: backgroundSampleData,","    numCoalitions: 300",")","","print(\"KernelSHAP Attributions: \\(attributions)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"},{"anchor":"3-Local-Surrogate-Explanations-with-LIME","text":"3. Local Surrogate Explanations with LIME","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer"},{"type":"text","text":" perturbs the target instance with Gaussian noise, queries the black-box model on the neighborhood, and trains an interpretable, locally-weighted ridge linear surrogate:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiftExplain","","let lime = LIMEExplainer(kernelWidth: 0.75, regularization: 1.0)","","let explanation = await lime.explain(","    model: { x in await complexPipeline.predictScore(x) },","    instance: testInstance,","    numSamples: 500",")","","print(\"Local Model Intercept: \\(explanation.intercept)\")","print(\"Local Surrogate Fidelity (R²): \\(String(format: \"%.3f\", explanation.localR2))\")","","for (idx, weight) in explanation.featureWeights.enumerated() {","    print(\"Feature \\(idx) Local Weight: \\(String(format: \"%.4f\", weight))\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"thematicBreak"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAPExplanation","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer"],"anchor":"Explainability-Engines","title":"Explainability Engines"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/shapleyattributions"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain"]]},"references":{"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/LIMEExplainer":{"abstract":[{"text":"Local Interpretable Model-agnostic Explanations (LIME).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/LIMEExplainer","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/limeexplainer","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LIMEExplainer"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LIMEExplainer"}],"type":"topic","title":"LIMEExplainer"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/TreeSHAPExplanation":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Explanation structure containing exact TreeSHAP attributions and baseline predictions."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAPExplanation","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/treeshapexplanation","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TreeSHAPExplanation","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TreeSHAPExplanation","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"TreeSHAPExplanation"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/KernelSHAP":{"fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KernelSHAP"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/KernelSHAP","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/kernelshap","type":"topic","title":"KernelSHAP","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model interpretation using the KernelSHAP algorithm."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KernelSHAP"}]},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/TreeSHAP":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/treeshap","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/TreeSHAP","title":"TreeSHAP","abstract":[{"text":"Fast, exact TreeSHAP (Tree Shapley Additive Explanations) for decision trees and tree ensembles","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Lundberg et al., 2018; Nature Machine Intelligence).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"TreeSHAP","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TreeSHAP","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain/ModelInterpretability":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain\/ModelInterpretability","abstract":[{"text":"Understand black-box machine learning predictions using ","type":"text"},{"code":"TreeSHAP","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"KernelSHAP","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"LIMEExplainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"PermutationImportance","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"PartialDependencePlot","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Model Interpretability & XAI Guide","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain\/modelinterpretability"},"doc://SwiftExplain/documentation/SwiftExplain":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftExplain\/documentation\/SwiftExplain","url":"\/documentation\/swiftexplain","role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Model Explainability, SHAP & Feature Attributions."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftExplain"}}}